{"claims":[{"claim":"Each hunk's behaviour follows from lessons verified earlier: truthiness of 0.0 (D3-L3), inner join drops unmatched rows (D3-L1), MERGE grain keys (A3, D4), self-confirming tests (D5-L3), secrets from the environment (D5-L3).","source":"Local runs recorded in the claims of the lessons named, September 2026.","status":"verified"}],"concept_html":"<p>This capstone brings Track D together. An assistant has opened pull request #214 against your pipeline repository. The full PR is in <code>practice/capstone/pr_review/PR.md</code>, with a review template beside it. The exercises below show the same five files, one per exercise, and a final verdict. The answer key stays hidden until you submit.</p>\n<p><strong>The PR's description</strong> says: \"All tests pass. The code follows the team standard and has been tested thoroughly.\" Treat every sentence as a claim to check, not a fact (lesson D6-L1).</p>\n<p><strong>Review each file with the full routine:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Goal.</strong> What does this change say it does? The docstring or the description tells you.</li>\n<li><strong>Read-through.</strong> Names, types, side effects and scope (D6-L1).</li>\n<li><strong>Known data.</strong> Work one small case by hand. Does the code give your answer (D6-L2)?</li>\n<li><strong>Assumptions.</strong> What must be true of the data for this to work? Is it true (D6-L3)?</li>\n<li><strong>Standard.</strong> Nulls and truthiness, join grain, MERGE keys, tests that repeat the code, secrets (D3, D5, D7).</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>For every finding, record four things:</strong> the line, the defect, whether it blocks the merge, and the fix you request. A finding without a requested fix is a complaint, not a review.</p>\n<p><strong>Grading.</strong> Each file is a spot-the-bug exercise. Tapping the right line counts as a bug found. A fix that passes the checker counts as a fix proposed. The last exercise asks for your verdict and the reasons behind it.</p>\n<p>Aim to find all five before you open a hint. Then compare your written review with the explanations. The defects missed most often in real reviews are the ones that run cleanly: a truthiness test, an inner join, a MERGE key and a test that repeats the code.</p>","example":{"language":"text","strong":{"lines":["Finding 1 (blocking): qa_statistical.py line 3 treats a 0.0 share as missing.","  Checked: stability_status(0.0, 0.12) returns SKIP, expected WARN.","  Fix: test `is not None` on both shares, and add a test for 0.0.","Verdict: request changes. 4 blocking findings, 1 security finding."],"notes":[{"html":"A worked example proves the finding.","line":2},{"html":"The verdict follows from the findings.","line":4}]},"takeaway_html":"<p>Every finding names the line, the defect, the severity, the check and the fix. The verdict follows from the findings.</p>","weak":{"lines":["Review: LGTM, tests pass."],"notes":[{"html":"Repeats the author's claim. No finding, no check, no fix.","line":1}]}},"exercises":[{"difficulty":1,"hints":["Lesson D6-L1: read before you trust.","What evidence backs each sentence?","Check each claim."],"hints_html":["Lesson D6-L1: read before you trust.","What evidence backs each sentence?","Check each claim."],"id":"X3-L1-E1","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Treat each as a claim, and check it against the diff and the tests"},{"id":"b","text":"Accept them and review only the style"},{"id":"c","text":"Ignore the description entirely"},{"id":"d","text":"Approve, since the suite is green"}],"options_html":{"a":"Treat each as a claim, and check it against the diff and the tests","b":"Accept them and review only the style","c":"Ignore the description entirely","d":"Approve, since the suite is green"},"prompt":"PR #214's description says \"All tests pass. The code follows the team standard and has been tested thoroughly.\" What do you do with these sentences?\n","prompt_html":"<p>PR #214's description says \"All tests pass. The code follows the team standard and has been tested thoroughly.\" What do you do with these sentences?</p>","reasons":[{"id":"r1","text":"A description states intent. Only the diff and the tests show what the code does."},{"id":"r2","text":"Assistants always write false descriptions."}],"reasons_html":{"r1":"A description states intent. Only the diff and the tests show what the code does.","r2":"Assistants always write false descriptions."},"sealed":"","type":"mcq","xp":10},{"code":"def stability_status(current_pct: float | None, prior_pct: float | None, tolerance: float = 0.10) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return WARN if the share moved more than tolerance, PASS if not, SKIP if missing.\"\"\"\n    if current_pct and prior_pct:\n        return \"WARN\" if abs(current_pct - prior_pct) > tolerance else \"PASS\"\n    return \"SKIP\"\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">stability_status</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">current_pct</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">float</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">prior_pct</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">float</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">tolerance</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">float</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.10</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>","<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"Return WARN if the share moved more than tolerance, PASS if not, SKIP if missing.\"\"\"</span>","    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">current_pct</span> <span class=\"ow\">and</span> <span class=\"n\">prior_pct</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>","        <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"WARN\"</span> <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"nb\">abs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">current_pct</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"n\">prior_pct</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"n\">tolerance</span> <span class=\"k\">else</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"PASS\"</span>","    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"SKIP\"</span>"],"difficulty":1,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":["Still a truthiness test. Compare with <code>is not None</code>."],"checks":[{"lines":["<span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">stability_status</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.12</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"WARN\"</span>"],"message_html":"A drop to 0.0 must WARN."},{"lines":["<span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">stability_status</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.12</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"SKIP\"</span>"],"message_html":"A missing share still returns SKIP."}],"include_html":[],"must_html":["A drop to 0.0 must WARN.","A missing share still returns SKIP."],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"ast_rules":[{"id":"no_truthiness","kind":"forbids_bare_truthiness","message":"Still a truthiness test. Compare with `is not None`.","names":["current_pct","prior_pct"]}],"kind":"python","setup":"","tests":[{"code":"assert stability_status(0.0, 0.12) == \"WARN\"\n","id":"zero","message":"A drop to 0.0 must WARN."},{"code":"assert stability_status(None, 0.12) == \"SKIP\"\n","id":"missing","message":"A missing share still returns SKIP."}]},"hints":["Work stability_status(0.0, 0.12) by hand.","0.0 is falsy.","`is not None` on both."],"hints_html":["Work stability_status(0.0, 0.12) by hand.","0.0 is falsy.","<code>is not None</code> on both."],"id":"X3-L1-E2","language":"python","packages":[],"prompt":"File 1, `qa_statistical.py`. Goal from the docstring: WARN if the share moved more than the tolerance, SKIP only if a share is missing. Find the defect and fix it.\n","prompt_html":"<p>File 1, <code>qa_statistical.py</code>. Goal from the docstring: WARN if the share moved more than the tolerance, SKIP only if a share is missing. Find the defect and fix it.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":10},{"code":"from pyspark.sql import functions as F\n\ndef add_region_names(gold: DataFrame, regions: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Attach region names. One row per gold row.\"\"\"\n    return gold.join(regions, \"region_code\")\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">pyspark.sql</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">functions</span> <span class=\"k\">as</span> <span class=\"n\">F</span>","","<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">add_region_names</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">gold</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">DataFrame</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">regions</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">DataFrame</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"n\">DataFrame</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>","<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"Attach region names. One row per gold row.\"\"\"</span>","    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">gold</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">regions</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"region_code\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>"],"difficulty":2,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":[],"checks":[],"include_html":["Use a left join: gold.join(regions, \"region_code\", \"left\")."],"must_html":[],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"ast_rules":[{"id":"left_join","kind":"requires_pattern","message":"Use a left join: gold.join(regions, \"region_code\", \"left\").","pattern":"join\\(\\s*(F\\.broadcast\\()?regions\\)?\\s*,\\s*[\"']region_code[\"']\\s*,\\s*(how\\s*=\\s*)?[\"']left[\"']"}],"kind":"python","setup":"","tests":[]},"hints":["What happens to gold rows whose code is not in regions?","The default join type is inner.","Use a left join."],"hints_html":["What happens to gold rows whose code is not in regions?","The default join type is inner.","Use a left join."],"id":"X3-L1-E3","language":"pyspark","packages":[],"prompt":"File 2, `gold_metrics.py`. Goal from the docstring: one row per gold row, with region names attached. Gold has region codes missing from the lookup. Find the defect and fix it.\n","prompt_html":"<p>File 2, <code>gold_metrics.py</code>. Goal from the docstring: one row per gold row, with region names attached. Gold has region codes missing from the lookup. Find the defect and fix it.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":20},{"code":"MERGE INTO research.research_silver.nat_respondents AS t\nUSING research.research_bronze.nat_latest AS s\nON t.respondent_id = s.respondent_id\nWHEN MATCHED THEN UPDATE SET *\nWHEN NOT MATCHED THEN INSERT *;\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"n\">MERGE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">INTO</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">research_silver</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat_respondents</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span>","<span class=\"k\">USING</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">research</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">research_bronze</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat_latest</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">AS</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span>","<span class=\"k\">ON</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respondent_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respondent_id</span>","<span class=\"k\">WHEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MATCHED</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">THEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">UPDATE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">SET</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span>","<span class=\"k\">WHEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">NOT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MATCHED</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">THEN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">INSERT</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">*</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>"],"difficulty":3,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":[],"checks":[],"include_html":["Match on both grain keys: respondent_id and wave_id."],"must_html":[],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"comments":"sql","kind":"text","rules":[{"id":"both_keys","message":"Match on both grain keys: respondent_id and wave_id.","pattern":"ON\\s+t\\.respondent_id\\s*=\\s*s\\.respondent_id\\s+AND\\s+t\\.wave_id\\s*=\\s*s\\.wave_id|ON\\s+t\\.wave_id\\s*=\\s*s\\.wave_id\\s+AND\\s+t\\.respondent_id\\s*=\\s*s\\.respondent_id","type":"required"}]},"hints":["What is silver's grain?","Which key is missing from the ON clause?","wave_id."],"hints_html":["What is silver's grain?","Which key is missing from the ON clause?","wave_id."],"id":"X3-L1-E4","language":"sql","packages":[],"prompt":"File 3, `silver_merge.sql`. Silver's grain is one row per respondent per wave. Find the defect and fix it.\n","prompt_html":"<p>File 3, <code>silver_merge.sql</code>. Silver's grain is one row per respondent per wave. Find the defect and fix it.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":30},{"code":"def test_stability_status():\n    current, prior, tol = 0.30, 0.10, 0.10\n    expected = \"WARN\" if abs(current - prior) > tol else \"PASS\"\n    assert stability_status(current, prior, tol) == expected\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">test_stability_status</span><span class=\"p\">():</span>","    <span class=\"n\">current</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">prior</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">tol</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.30</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.10</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"mf\">0.10</span>","    <span class=\"n\">expected</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"WARN\"</span> <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"nb\">abs</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">current</span> <span class=\"o\">-</span> <span class=\"n\">prior</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"n\">tol</span> <span class=\"k\">else</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"PASS\"</span>","    <span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">stability_status</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">current</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">prior</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">tol</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"n\">expected</span>"],"difficulty":3,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":["The expected value must not repeat the formula. Write the answer by hand."],"checks":[],"include_html":["Assert a literal expected value, such as == \"WARN\".","Add the case that the code gets wrong: a current share of 0.0."],"must_html":[],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"ast_rules":[{"id":"no_formula","kind":"forbids_pattern","message":"The expected value must not repeat the formula. Write the answer by hand.","pattern":"abs\\("},{"id":"literal_warn","kind":"requires_pattern","message":"Assert a literal expected value, such as == \"WARN\".","pattern":"==\\s*[\"']WARN[\"']"},{"id":"zero_case","kind":"requires_pattern","message":"Add the case that the code gets wrong: a current share of 0.0.","pattern":"stability_status\\(\\s*0\\.0\\s*,"}],"kind":"python","setup":"","tests":[]},"hints":["Where does the expected value come from?","From the same formula as the code.","Write literal answers, including 0.0."],"hints_html":["Where does the expected value come from?","From the same formula as the code.","Write literal answers, including 0.0."],"id":"X3-L1-E5","language":"python","packages":[],"prompt":"File 4, `test_qa_statistical.py`. The description says \"all tests pass\". Find the line that makes this test worthless, and rewrite the test with hand-worked expected values, including the 0.0 case.\n","prompt_html":"<p>File 4, <code>test_qa_statistical.py</code>. The description says \"all tests pass\". Find the line that makes this test worthless, and rewrite the test with hand-worked expected values, including the 0.0 case.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":30},{"code":"import requests\n\nAPI_TOKEN = \"tok_EXAMPLE_not_real_0000\"\n\ndef fetch_wave(wave_id: str) -> dict[str, object]:\n    \"\"\"Fetch wave metadata from the survey platform.\"\"\"\n    headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {API_TOKEN}\"}\n    return requests.get(f\"https://survey.example/api/waves/{wave_id}\", headers=headers, timeout=30).json()\n","code_lines":["<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">requests</span>","","<span class=\"n\">API_TOKEN</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"tok_EXAMPLE_not_real_0000\"</span>","","<span class=\"k\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">fetch_wave</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">wave_id</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">-&gt;</span> <span class=\"nb\">dict</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">object</span><span class=\"p\">]:</span>","<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"sd\">\"\"\"Fetch wave metadata from the survey platform.\"\"\"</span>","    <span class=\"n\">headers</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Authorization\"</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"Bearer </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">API_TOKEN</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">}</span>","    <span class=\"k\">return</span> <span class=\"n\">requests</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://survey.example/api/waves/</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">wave_id</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">headers</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">headers</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">30</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">json</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>"],"difficulty":4,"fix_brief":{"avoid_html":["Remove the literal token from the code."],"checks":[],"include_html":["Read os.environ[\"SURVEY_API_TOKEN\"] inside the function.","Import os."],"must_html":[],"shape":[],"shape_note":"","steps_html":["Change only the line you marked, and the lines it affects.","Keep the rest of the code as it is.","Tap Run checks. A failed check tells you what is still wrong."]},"fix_checker":{"ast_rules":[{"id":"no_literal","kind":"forbids_pattern","message":"Remove the literal token from the code.","pattern":"tok_EXAMPLE"},{"id":"from_env","kind":"requires_pattern","message":"Read os.environ[\"SURVEY_API_TOKEN\"] inside the function.","pattern":"os\\.environ\\[\\s*[\"']SURVEY_API_TOKEN[\"']\\s*\\]|os\\.environ\\.get\\(\\s*[\"']SURVEY_API_TOKEN[\"']|os\\.getenv\\(\\s*[\"']SURVEY_API_TOKEN[\"']"},{"id":"imports_os","kind":"requires_import","message":"Import os.","module":"os"}],"kind":"python","setup":"","tests":[]},"hints":["Which line puts a credential into Git?","A literal token.","Read it from the environment at call time."],"hints_html":["Which line puts a credential into Git?","A literal token.","Read it from the environment at call time."],"id":"X3-L1-E6","language":"python","packages":[],"prompt":"File 5, `wave_api.py`. Find the security defect and fix it: read the token from the environment variable `SURVEY_API_TOKEN` at call time.\n","prompt_html":"<p>File 5, <code>wave_api.py</code>. Find the security defect and fix it: read the token from the environment variable <code>SURVEY_API_TOKEN</code> at call time.</p>","sealed":"","type":"spot_bug","xp":40},{"difficulty":5,"hints":["How many findings block the merge?","What does the only test actually check?","Targeted fixes or a restart?"],"hints_html":["How many findings block the merge?","What does the only test actually check?","Targeted fixes or a restart?"],"id":"X3-L1-E7","prompt":"Write the verdict section of your review.\n","prompt_html":"<p>Write the verdict section of your review.</p>","sealed":"","slots":[{"answer":"changes","id":"verdict","label":"Verdict","options":[{"id":"changes","text":"Request changes"},{"id":"approve_comments","text":"Approve with comments"},{"id":"approve","text":"Approve"}]},{"answer":"unsupported","id":"claims","label":"The description's 'all tests pass'","options":[{"id":"unsupported","text":"True but meaningless: the only test repeats the code, so passing proves nothing"},{"id":"supported","text":"Supports approval: the suite is green"}]},{"answer":"fixes_tests","id":"ask","label":"What you ask the author for","options":[{"id":"fixes_tests","text":"Fixes for all five findings, hand-worked tests including 0.0 and a multi-wave respondent, and the assumptions behind each change"},{"id":"rewrite","text":"A complete rewrite of the PR"}]}],"type":"design","xp":50}],"id":"X3-L1","module":"X3","practical":null,"recap":[{"back":"Line, defect, blocking or not, how you checked it, and the fix you request.","front":"Five parts of a review finding","id":"X3-L1#0"},{"back":"Truthiness of 0.0, an inner join breaking grain, a MERGE missing wave_id, a self-confirming test, a token in code.","front":"Defects this PR hid","id":"X3-L1#1"},{"back":"Every sentence is a claim. 'All tests pass' needs the tests to be read.","front":"Treating a PR description","id":"X3-L1#2"}],"tags":["all-months"],"title":"Capstone 3: review an AI-generated pull request","track":"X","why_html":"<p>More of the code you review will be written by assistants. It arrives with confident descriptions and passing tests. A reviewer who checks the claims, works an example by hand and reads the tests as critically as the code is what keeps those pull requests from quietly corrupting a pipeline.</p>"}
